# 004 — Security & Data Isolation

## 1. Zero Credential Leakage
- Never log authorization tokens, passwords, cookies, or PII to console or telemetry.
- Never hardcode personal addresses or secret keys into source code or security rules.

## 2. Runtime Schema Validation
- All boundary inputs (HTTP request bodies, query params, headers, webhooks, environment variables) MUST be validated with a strict runtime schema parser (e.g. Zod) before being processed.
- Discard or reject unknown/extra fields by default (`.strict()` parsing).

## 3. Multi-Tenant & Session Isolation
- Always enforce tenant and user boundaries at the data query level (e.g. `WHERE tenant_id = ? AND user_id = ?`).
- Prohibit wildcard administrative reads from public-facing endpoints.
